-- title:
--   Greenberg–Wiles inequality: strict at S, relaxed at Q
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $S$ and $Q$ be finite sets of primes which are disjoint and with $p \in S$ (as the element `pPrime p`), and let $M$ be a representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ which is finite-dimensional, satisfies the smoothness condition that each $m \in M$ is fixed by the fixing subgroup of some intermediate field $F$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ finite over $\mathbb{Q}$, and is unramified outside $S \cup Q$ in the sense that for every prime $q \notin S \cup Q$ and every valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, every element of the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ acts on $M$ as the identity. Write $M' =$ `M.dualTwist (cycloChar p)` for the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-dual of $M$ with action twisted by the mod $p$ cyclotomic character, for each prime $q$ let `primeLocalToGlobal q` be the homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}_q}/\mathbb{Q}_q) \to \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ obtained by restricting scalars to $\mathbb{Q}$ and then restricting to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let `archimedeanLoc` be the inclusion of the subgroup generated by complex conjugation, and for a representation $N$ let `continuousH1S (S ∪ Q) N` be the submodule of $H^1$ of classes represented by cocycles in `levelCocyclesS₁ (S ∪ Q) N`, and `continuousH1 (primeLocalToGlobal q) N` the submodule of classes represented by cocycles in `levelCocycles₁ (primeLocalToGlobal q) N`. Then, with all ranks taken over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, the rank of the intersection of `continuousH1S (S ∪ Q) M` with the kernels of the restriction maps $H^1(\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}), M) \to H^1(\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}_q}/\mathbb{Q}_q), M)$ for all $q \in S$, plus the rank of the invariants of $M'$, plus the rank of the invariants of $M$ under the subgroup generated by complex conjugation, plus the sum over $q \in S \cup Q$ of the ranks of the invariants of $M$ under $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}_q}/\mathbb{Q}_q)$, is at most the rank of the intersection of `continuousH1S (S ∪ Q) M'` with the kernels of the restriction maps at all $q \in Q$, plus the rank of the invariants of $M$, plus the sum over $q \in Q$ of the ranks of `continuousH1 (primeLocalToGlobal q) M`.
--
--   This is the Greenberg–Wiles (Poitou–Tate) Euler characteristic formula, specialised to the local conditions that are strict at the primes of $S$ and unrestricted at the primes of $Q$ and at the archimedean place, and stated as an inequality in which the dual Selmer group is relaxed at $S$ and strict at $Q$. It is the form in which the formula enters the Taylor–Wiles method, and it is used to bound the strict Selmer group of a residual representation in terms of the number of Taylor–Wiles primes and the dual Selmer group.
